hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1060","From us Muhammad bin Hisham, from us Ismail, meaning Ibn Ulayya, on the authority of Khaled, on the authority of Abu Qalaba, on the authority of Abu Al-Muhallab, on the authority of Imran bin Husayn The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, “prostrated in my prostration of delusion.”"
"1061","Yusuf bin Musa told us, Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Abdullah, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Suwayd, he said: Alqamah led us in the noon prayer, and he prayed five times. When he greeted, the people said: O Abu Shibl, you have prayed five times. He said: No, as you did. They said: Yes, he said: So I was in the people’s side and I was a boy. So I said: Yes, you have prayed five times. He said to me: And you too, one-eyed man, say that? I said: Yes, so he approached, prostrated two prostrations, then said the salaam, then said: Abdullah said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, led us in prayer five times, and when the whispering of the people among them stopped, he said: “What’s the matter with you?” They said: O Messenger of God, did he add anything to the prayer? He said: “No.” They said: “You have prayed five times.” So he turned around and prostrated two prostrations, then gave the salutation. Then he said: “It was only \I am human. I forget just as you forget.\"""""
